Subject: windows.ui.xaml: IItemContainerMapping, AcrylicBrush, and framework types newer than XBF's table

ItemsControl, ListView and GridView implement IItemContainerMapping (ItemFromContainer, ContainerFromItem,
IndexFromContainer, ContainerFromIndex); an ItemsControl's containers are now remembered for it.

AcrylicBrush (a XamlCompositionBrushBase) keeps all its properties and draws the way Windows draws it with
transparency effects off: as its FallbackColor at the brush's Opacity. It can be created from code (composable)
and markup.

A framework type that XBF's table of built-in types doesn't have (AcrylicBrush is newer) comes in compiled markup
with the presentation namespace; such types are now created as built-ins instead of being asked of the app.

